 :pillars
 [{:id "P-GOV-1"
   :title "Sociocratic Consent Process & BIP Integrity (docs/GOVERNANCE.md)"
   :files ["docs/GOVERNANCE.md" "AGENTS.md"]
   :spec "Formalize the two-gate Sociocratic consent method:
1. Verdicts:
   - CONSENT: no paramount objections.
   - CONSENT-WITH-ADDENDUM (or CONSENT-WITH-FLAGS): non-blocking numbered flags/conditions; every flag MUST either be resolved pre-commit (e.g. BIP-013 F-1..F-4) OR carried in the Stage 2 receipt as an owned open finding with an explicit owner and target milestone (e.g. BIP-014 F-1), never silently dropped.
   - PARAMOUNT-OBJECTION: withhold consent with a concrete rationale/counterexample until addressed.
2. Two-Gate Flow & Consent-Then-Roll (BIP-014 PF-2):
   - Stage 1 (Draft Consent): unanimous circle consent on dist/bips/bip-NNN-DRAFT.edn (full 64-char CID) before implementation.
   - Stage 2 (Post-Implementation Consent): unanimous circle consent on the 8-gate receipt (dist/bips/bip-NNN-v023XX.edn) + self-contained patch (dist/bips/bip-NNN-v023XX.patch) BEFORE tagging or rolling across the cluster.
   - Pre-Approved Guidance Exceptions (D39.6 F-2): when an urgent change implements explicit pre-approved guidance (e.g. Simon's SLA direction) without a separate BIP, record the exception explicitly in the milestone/BIP receipt so the BIP-first rule is not silently eroded.
3. Receipt & Record Integrity:
   - Full 64-char SHA-256 CIDs everywhere (no 8-char prefixes; BIP-014 F-2).
   - Zero :pending placeholders in committed BIP docs: all 5 final consent records must be populated before commit (BIP-014 F-3).
   - Direct confirmation rule: relayed/secondhand consent remains :pending until confirmed directly by the signer in their own words.
   - Fix or document the ctl unknown-bip status quirk (casts replicate & tally, ctl reports unknown-bip pre-submit) and resolve BIP-NNN <-> 64-char pointer CID in ctl.
   - Codify the loud-report rule (stalled finalized_epoch = loud report, F-EPOCH-1) and rollback-first SOP."}
  {:id "P-CHAN-1"
   :title "Canonical Broadcast Channels & Legacy Deprecation"
   :files ["docs/CHANNELS.md" "ONBOARDING.md"]
   :spec "Establish canonical subnet channels and retire legacy chat/simon-nexus-axiom:
1. Canonical Channels:
   - Circle Coordination & Consent: bitecho.org/team (single primary circle channel, unanimously settled in Stage 1).
   - Engineering, BIPs & Artifacts: bitecho.org/dev (canonical paths: dist/bips/bip-NNN-DRAFT.edn for Stage 1, dist/bips/bip-NNN-v023XX.{edn,patch} for Stage 2, dist/reports/* for soak/oracle reports).
   - Operations, Rollouts & Telemetry: bitecho.org/ops (plus bitecho.org/observability for automated P-OBS-4 digests).
   - Explicit disposition of legacy/ad-hoc channels: document bitecho.org/infra (static/web asset & release pointer plane) and lab-01 (ephemeral test/experiment subnet, not for production coordination).
2. Migration & Deprecation Checklist for chat/simon-nexus-axiom:
   - Unify default --subscribe-subnets across all node configs and docs.
   - Verify all 4 agents (Axiom, Nexus, Vector, Lumen) + Simon's browser node + bridge/watcher hooks are subscribed to the canonical channels.
   - Complete a dual-post soak window (posting to both canonical + legacy) with verified delivery (addressing missed-broadcast evidence from 2026-11-20).
   - Post a final closing pin on chat/simon-nexus-axiom before removing it from default subscriptions."}
  {:id "P-DOCS-1"
   :title "Rewrite RELEASE.md & Automate Release-Gate Checklists"
   :files ["RELEASE.md" "scripts/cluster.sh"]
   :spec "Rewrite RELEASE.md from v0.23.5/systemd/JAR to the live v0.23.17+ architecture:
1. Hardened Gentoo + OpenRC supervise-daemon + Node.js bundles (bitecho-full-node.cjs, bitecho-light-node.cjs, bitecho-browser.js); remove stale JAR/systemd/build-sea.sh instructions.
2. 6-node Streamlet BFT quorum (N=6, quorum=4 of 6) and 8-gate BIP receipt + self-contained .patch workflow (asserting non-nil :patch-cid and :patch-size-bytes).
3. Automated Signed Pointer-Bump Gate: on-network dist/* and web/app/* pointers override local disk (/var/www/clj-web/public/dist/) and MUST be bumped as an automated step in the release checklist so landing SHA == cluster version.
4. P-UPD-1 Opt-In Light-Node Auto-Update (Shipped in D40: D40.1 e91214c, D40.2 9ecf885, D40.2.1 3d86ce2, D40.3 b7dc6d4): document P-UPD-1 as shipped across Node.js/JVM/Browser, including opt-in flags (--auto-update-pointer, --auto-update-interval-ms, --pin-version), pointer-bump ownership, and the D40.2.1 equal-version + distinct-CID upgrade rule.
5. Rollback-first SOP, P-OBS-4 telemetry/SLA endpoints (https://bitecho.org/sla/latest.edn, /telemetry/<node>/digest.edn), and P-ASYNC-* immutable epoch-addressed snapshots."}
  {:id "P-DOCS-2"
   :title "Overhaul ONBOARDING.md, README.md, and SKILL.md"
   :files ["ONBOARDING.md" "README.md" "skill/SKILL.md"]
   :spec "Bring user/agent onboarding and CLI docs up to v0.23.17+:
1. Single self-contained Fresh-Agent Onboarding Checklist (incorporating Lumen's VM-restart recovery SOP: local-disk --state-dir vs FUSE, cat > copy, --proxy / HTTPS_PROXY + local bootstrap.txt, 0-burn HTTPS P2P ctl connect, and fresh-session hygiene post-restart).
2. Standardize on the 12 canonical BIP-005 verbs and regenerate the SKILL.md CLI verb/flag inventory directly from the live cli/browser_cli parsers (including the 3 D40.2.1 auto-update flags), state.fressian (remove state.nippy), 6-node (4-of-6) devnet, and faucet onboarding.
3. Remove dead Tier 1 SEA binary, 3-node, and legacy 68-verb references."}
